# Atomic map replace (served by mower_map map_server_node at /map_server_node/replace_areas).
#
# The WHOLE area set in one call: map_server builds it off to the side, validates every
# area, then swaps it in under its lock with one rebuild and one save. On any error
# nothing changes (success=false, message says which area and why). No half-built map is
# ever published or used by the boundary check (field 2026-10-21: the GUI's
# clear_map + add_area x N let outside_m read 23 m mid-reload).
#
# areas               the new set, in areas.dat order (obstacles + obstacle_info as in
#                     add_area). An area is a navigation area (drawn path) when
#                     area.is_navigation_area or is_navigation_area[i] is true.
# is_navigation_area  optional, index-aligned with areas (empty = use the MapArea flag)
# channel_json        optional, index-aligned: set_area_channel settings_json of a
#                     navigation area ('' = none)
# settings_json       optional, index-aligned: set_area_settings JSON of that area
#                     ('' = keep: settings of an area re-added with the same name, or
#                     renamed with the same polygon, are carried over; settings of
#                     areas no longer present are dropped)
# The existing clear_map / add_area / set_area_channel services keep working.
mowgli_interfaces/MapArea[] areas
bool[] is_navigation_area
string[] channel_json
string[] settings_json
---
bool success
string message
